*.log
# Evidence logs are the exception: summarize_benchmarks.py, summarize_phase1.py and
# summarize_training_rate.py parse exactly these to rebuild the published artifacts in benchmarks/,
# so a clone without them cannot reproduce any number that the README quotes from them. New
# experiment logs stay ignored. The root-level ones moved into logs/ (2026-10-17); the openai_walker
# records stay beside the subproject that produced them.
!logs/eval_phase3_*.log
!logs/ars_evidence.log
!logs/dreamer_smoke.log
!logs/redq_evidence.log
!logs/dreamer_n16_250k_evidence.log
!openai_walker/eval_phase4_20ep.log
!openai_walker/eval_phase4_50ep.log
!openai_walker/eval_extratrees_50ep.log
# The GAIL retrain's stdout is the training-side record summarize_benchmarks.py parses for
# benchmarks/phase4_gail_retrain.json; the June run's equivalent survives only as its mlflow
# record, which is exported into benchmarks/gail_june_run_true_env_reward.json.
!openai_walker/gail_retrain_2026-10-05.log
# Launcher logs from the detached chains. They are the only primary source for the wall clocks that
# benchmarks/*.json record as literals (a training run's seconds are not reconstructable from its
# checkpoints), and %TEMP% gets cleaned without asking, so they live in the repository. One per
# chain, and tests/test_physics_presets.py recomputes the recorded spans from them.
!logs/chain*_evidence.log
!logs/chain*_gpu_samples.log
runs/
checkpoints/
# MPC demonstrations are ~7 MB of trajectory arrays per collection, and the planner is not
# bit-reproducible (its constraint solver jitters), so re-collecting would not return these bytes.
# What is versioned is the sidecar .json: seeds, config, per-episode outcomes and the observation
# normaliser, which is everything `bench_bc_teacher.py`'s committed result needs to be attributable.
benchmarks/demos/*.npz
# The trainers' --capture-video output lands here; it is evidence to look at, not to version, and
# the renderings used to check a claim are re-derivable from the checkpoint plus the eval seed.
videos/
*.pt
*.pth
*.pkl
*.zip
.env.local
# One pattern for every local interpreter: .venv, .venv-mjx, .venv-phase4 and the
# .venv-py38-backup kept when the primary venv moved from Python 3.8 to 3.11.
.venv*/
venv/
env/
*mlrun*
*.db
*.png
bench_*.json
temp_race_env.xml
# Written beside a model file by bench_mjx.build_mjx() so an <include>-based scene can be compiled
# with the <size> capacities MJX needs. Derived text, not source.
_mjx_sized_*.xml
# One per batch size, written by bench_mjx's sweep subprocess and read back by the parent.
_mjx_scratch_single_*.json

# Generated by envs.walker_ragdoll_env.resolve_contact_world(): the <pair> variants of
# walker_ragdoll.xml, rebuilt on demand. Derived files, not source.
.contact_worlds/

# Third-party model files fetched for measurement, never vendored: the Menagerie
# Unitree G1 is 36 MB of STL meshes, and the point of measuring it here is the cost, not a copy.
# benchmarks/g1_native_cost.json records the upstream commit and each file hash it was measured from.
external/
